<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78596" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπλέω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπλευρ-πλώω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Orph.
			<u>A.</u>
			733
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			1271
		</span></i> : 
			Ep.
		
		aor. 2
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρέπλων</span> (v. infr.) :—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sail by</i> or <i>past</i>,
			abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴη δὴ κείνῃ γε παρέπλω . .
				Ἀργώ</span> was the only ship that <i>sailed through</i>
			that way, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.69
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.1.11
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν χρῷ παραπλέοντες</span>
			<i>sailing close in</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.84
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				90
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. παρὰ τὰς πρῴρας τῶν νεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.100
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὴν Ἔφεσον</span>
			<i>sail past</i> Ephesus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				20.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>coast by</i> or <i>along</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃς τῆς Ἀττικῆς ταῦτα μὴ -πέπλωκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.99
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				15.123
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς Σικυῶνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.111
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθένδε μὲν εἰς Σινώπην π., ἐκ
					Σινώπης δὲ εἰς Ἡράκλειαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.6.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				35.31
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεῖθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					5.4.61
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀπὸ κάλω</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλως</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὰς συμφοράς</span>
			<i>sail past, escape</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Amphis
				3.4
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
